diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 56a6f74..f3dc1ae 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@
 # AEmulator 0.0.0.3
 
+### Root and modules (this fork, ported from the foreign VMOS app)
+- **Working root for guest apps**: the guest tree ships a plain `su` script (/system/bin, /system/xbin, /sbin); every call becomes a request file that a new host-side daemon (core/SuDaemon.kt) runs as a uid-0 guest process and answers with output + exit code. No kernel, no Magisk, works on every engine (2.3–4.4 QEMU and the native arm64 one).
+- **Superuser panel** (VM menu → Superuser): master root switch, default policy (grant all / ask each / deny all), per-app allow/deny rules, the log of recent requests; "ask" requests pop a dialog in the VM window (60 s of silence = deny). Rules persist next to the image.
+- **Xposed module management** (VM menu → Modules): module APKs are installed into the guest as regular apps and registered (enabled/disabled, version); with an enabled module the boot seeds the framework markers the module/checker apps look for (xposed.prop, XposedBridge.jar). The LSPlant in-process loader that applies modules to scoped apps is the next phase; the registry it will consume is live.
+- **APK install fixed**: the "Install APK" menu item pushed the file to the emulated sdcard, which the guest's own pm refuses (like real Android refuses /storage paths) — the dialog then always said "install failed". Now the APK lands in the image's /data/local/tmp (the exact path of the `adb install` that worked) and is installed over the same channel, with pm's real output in the toast.
+
